          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "てにもつ (tenimotsu) is built from both layers of the vocabulary: the native Japanese (wago) te, \"hand\", inherited rather than borrowed; the native Japanese (wago) ni, \"load\", inherited rather than borrowed; and the Sino-Japanese motsu, \"thing\" (Middle Chinese mjut), an on'yomi borrowed from Chinese (JMdict; KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
